# ============================================================
#  THE HOLLOW STAR: the acts' openers, climaxes and confrontations (v2, docs/plots/hollowstar-v2.md).
#  The wiring (act threads, deadlines, the Night) is in content/events/hollowstar/threads.grim; the newer cards are
#  in content/events/hollowstar/. The beats are deadlines: each act's climax raises the clock to the next opener.
#  Act I (omens)            opener hs_lake_breathes (beat 1)
#  Act II (investigation)   opener hs_ilse_arrives (beat 4), with hs_silver_rings and hs_seraphine_towers; climax
#                           hs_frost_ring (beat 5); hs_ilse_door is one of its steps
#  Act III (escalation)     opener hs_dark_tower (beat 7); hs_two_shadows -> hs_choosing_sides; hs_maud_locks
#  Act IV (convergence)     opener hs_last_winter (beat 10): who stands with you beneath the lake
# ============================================================

# ---------------- Act I: omens ----------------

@event hs_lake_breathes
title: The Lake Breathes
arc: hollowstar
beat: 1
slot: evening
class: story
tone: eerie
art: snow
tags: mystery hollowstar
thread: hs_omens
scene: The Great Hall at supper, every head turned to the tall windows, the lake beyond them gone white with sudden frost.
text: At supper the lake outside the tall windows goes white in one breath, and every candle in the Great Hall leans toward it. Far under the water a bell tolls. Professor Thorne's spoon freezes into his soup. The headmistress rises. "A cold current," she says pleasantly. "Eat." Then the lake breathes out, and is water again. Nobody eats.
> left: Run down to the shore
  meet maud
  find lead_lake_breathed
  find lead_maud_friend
  queue hs_dreams_begin within 1..3
  health -tiny
  say: The shore is soaked and freezing, and the reeds are white to the root. Old Maud is already there with a lantern, staring at the water. "Last time it did that, I lost a friend," she says, not quite to you. Then she sends you to bed, sharply, and you go.
> right: Follow Thorne out of the hall
  find lead_founders_archive
  queue hs_dreams_begin within 1..3
  lore +tiny
  mood -tiny
  say: Thorne leaves his frozen soup and walks straight to the library archive, fast for a man of his age. You hear the vault door slam. You lie awake wondering what he went down there to read.

# ---------------- Act II: the Wardens stir ----------------

@event hs_silver_rings
title: Silver at Supper
arc: hollowstar
beat: 4
slot: night
class: story
tone: eerie
art: ring
tags: mystery hollowstar
thread: hs_investigation
scene: The Great Hall at supper, candlelight catching three identical silver rings on three very different hands at the high table.
text: At supper you notice three identical silver rings at the high table: on the headmistress, on Professor Thorne and on Old Maud's earthy hand. After curfew, from your window, you see all three walking the lakeshore with lanterns, stopping at the foot of each tower in turn.
> left: Follow them down
  challenge deceive vs thorne.guile:
    win:
      lore +small
      say: You shadow them from tower to tower. At each one they lay a palm on the stone and wait. At the last, Maud takes her hand away and blows on her fingers as if the wall were ice.
    lose:
      mood -small
      rel thorne -small
      say: A lantern swings toward you. "Hm," says Professor Thorne. "Bed." He doesn't report you, which somehow feels worse.
> right: Draw the curtains
  health +small
  mood -tiny
  say: You sleep well, mostly. In the morning the rings are still there at breakfast, and nobody at the high table looks as if they slept at all.

@event hs_seraphine_towers
title: Seven, Then Six
arc: hollowstar
beat: 4
slot: night
class: story
tone: eerie
actor: seraphine
art: tower
tags: mystery hollowstar
thread: hs_investigation
scene: A seer on the observatory balcony at night, counting the academy's towers on her fingers, one finger held back.
text: Seraphine is on the observatory balcony, counting towers on her fingers. "Seven," she says. "Seven. Six, and then… no. Seven, for now." She looks at you as if you had arrived a little early. "What month is it? I lose track around the… you know."
> left: "Which one goes out?"
  lore +small
  mood -small
  find lead_seventh_tower
  say: She points, then frowns at her own hand. "That one. Or the one next to it. Next year, I think. Not the seventh; nobody's lit the seventh for a hundred years." She doesn't remember saying it the next morning, but you do.
> right: "It's {month}. Evening."
  rel seraphine +medium
  mood +tiny
  say: She lets out a long breath and sits down on the cold stone. "Thank you. I was halfway into a winter." You stay until she is sure which one she's in.

@event hs_ilse_arrives
title: A Storm at the Gate
arc: hollowstar
beat: 4
slot: noon
when: met(kael)
class: story
tone: tense
actor: kael
art: snow
tags: mystery hollowstar
thread: hs_investigation
# Act II's opener (v2): Ilse arrives, and the Dumonts clash in the open.
scene: A snowstorm falling on one girl in white furs in the middle of a sunny courtyard, a pale young man facing her, students scattering, a cracked fountain between them.
text: At noon a snowstorm walks in through the academy gate, with a girl in white furs at the middle of it. Kael drops his books. "Go home, Ilse." "Make me." They shout at each other across the courtyard in Northern, and the fountain between them cracks in half. Half the school is watching. Then she turns on her heel and goes, down the road to the village.
> left: Go after her
  flag ilse_in_village
  find lead_white_furs
  queue ilse_village in 1
  rel kael -tiny
  mood -tiny
  say: Kael catches your sleeve. "Don't. She's here for the door, not for me." He lets go when you don't stop. By the time you reach the road the snow has stopped too, and there's only a line of frozen footprints toward the bakery.
> right: Stay with Kael
  flag ilse_in_village
  find lead_white_furs
  rel kael +small
  say: You pick up his books. He stands looking at the broken fountain until the bell goes. "My sister," he says at last. "She's taken a room above the bakery. She isn't here to visit."

@event hs_frost_ring
title: Things Come Ashore
arc: hollowstar
beat: 5
slot: night
when: since(hs_ilse_arrives) >= 2
type: menu
class: story
tone: tense
art: snow
tags: mystery hollowstar danger
thread: hs_investigation
# Act II's climax (v2): two of the act's truths bring it early (hs_investigation_progress), the deadline otherwise; it
# opens Act III. The fight is one way through; watching the headmistress and herding the first-years are the others.
scene: The Mirror Lake on a warm night, a perfect white ring of frost on the water, figures of frost and whispers climbing onto the shore, a tall woman with a lantern facing them.
on_show:
  advance hollowstar to 7
text: {season == "winter": A still, starless night|A warm night}, and a ring of frost as wide as the Great Hall has formed in the middle of the lake. Far below, the bell tolls, and tolls. Then things climb out of the ring onto the shore: shapes of frost and whispers, walking like people who have forgotten how. The headmistress stands alone at the waterline with a lantern, talking to the lake.
> fight: Meet them on the shore
  hint: Combat. Kael fights beside you, if he's your ally.
  if flag(kael_ally):
    challenge combat adept+ drift mid with kael:
      win:
        renown +small
        alignment +tiny
        find lake_bell
        say: Kael's frost and your spells meet the first of them on the shingle, and it comes apart into snow and a sound like someone saying your name. The rest turn back to the water. Under the ice, as it closes, you hear the bell's note clearly for the first time.
      lose:
        mood -small
        say: It walks through your spell as if it were weather and puts a cold hand on your chest, and you can't breathe for a long moment. Kael drags you back up the shingle. When you can see again, the ring has closed and the shapes are gone.
  else:
    challenge combat adept+ drift mid:
      win:
        renown +small
        alignment +tiny
        find lake_bell
        say: Your spell meets the first of them on the shingle, and it comes apart into snow and a sound like someone saying your name. The rest turn back to the water. Under the ice, as it closes, you hear the bell's note clearly for the first time.
      lose:
        mood -small
        say: It walks through your spell as if it were weather and puts a cold hand on your chest, and you can't breathe for a long moment. When you can see again, the ring has closed, the shapes are gone, and the headmistress is helping you up.
> watch: Watch what she does
  hint: Guile. She doesn't like an audience.
  challenge deceive expert likely:
    win:
      find lake_bell
      lore +small
      say: She kneels and speaks to the water, slow and patient, the way you'd speak to a sleeping animal. The shapes stop on the shingle and listen. The ring shrinks, cracks, and is gone, and the bell under it rings one long note you'll know again anywhere.
    lose:
      rel isolde +tiny
      mood -small
      say: "Good evening," she says, without turning round, as a shape of frost walks past her into the lake. "You are the third student this week. The other two asked questions." She tells you nothing, and remembers your name.
> help: Get the first-years inside
  hint: Nobody will see what happens at the water.
  renown +small
  rel isolde +small
  health -tiny
  say: You run the length of the first-year tower banging on doors, and get forty children into the common room and the shutters closed. Something taps on the glass all night, very politely. In the morning there are wet footprints on the stairs, going up.

# ---------------- Act III: escalation ----------------

@event hs_dark_tower
title: The Tower That Went Dark
arc: hollowstar
beat: 7
when: since(hs_frost_ring) >= 2
class: story
tone: grim
art: candle
tags: mystery hollowstar danger
thread: hs_escalation
# Act III's opener (v2): the cult strikes, in the open.
scene: An academy tower standing black against the night sky among its lit neighbours, a black star burned into a great wooden door, and below them a lake half-covered in ice.
text: Mid-lecture, every lamp in the Lecture Tower goes out at once, and none of them will light again. In the morning there's a black star burned into the door of the Great Hall, still smoking, and half the lake has frozen {season == "winter": black and glassy, harder than any winter ice|weeks before any frost}, in a sheet that ends in a clean edge, as if cut. Out on it, at dawn, someone in black furs is walking away.
> left: Go after the figure on the ice
  hint: Nerve. The ice is thinner than it looks.
  challenge feat expert:
    win:
      lore +medium
      health -small
      say: You follow the footprints to the middle of the ice, where they simply stop. Under your boots the ice is clear as glass. Far down, something round and dark sits on the lakebed, and a glow runs along its rim. Then the glow turns, slowly, as if to look up.
    lose:
      health -medium
      say: The ice groans and a crack races past your feet. You scramble back to the shore soaked to the knee, and a prefect writes your name down very slowly. The figure in black furs never once looks back.
> right: Carry lamps for the prefects
  renown +small
  health -tiny
  say: You spend the night carrying lamps up the Lecture Tower stairs. Every one goes out at the doorway. The first-years have started sleeping in their clothes. From her window across the courtyard, the headmistress watches you try.

@event hs_maud_locks
title: Maud Has Seen Ice Before
when: seen(hs_dark_tower) > 0
class: story
tone: eerie
actor: maud
weight: 16
art: cup
tags: mystery hollowstar
thread: hs_escalation
scene: An old woman wrapped in a shawl on her cottage step, two mugs steaming beside her, a tall woman in dark robes walking stiffly away down the path, a half-frozen lake beyond.
text: At Maud's gate the headmistress is saying, quite pleasantly, "Keep the young ones out of it, Maud." "No," says Maud, "and you know why." The headmistress walks away very straight. Maud pushes a mug of tea at you. "{season == "winter": It doesn't freeze like that, dearie, not even in winter|The lake doesn't freeze this time of year, dearie}. Sixty years ago it did, and three of us went down. Sit. Or ask."
> left: Sit with her
  rel maud +medium
  mood -tiny
  say: You drink your tea and watch the ice. She hums something old. When the mugs are empty she squeezes your hand. "That was the right one," she says, and you'll only understand why much later.
> right: Ask what's holding it shut
  find seven_locks
  find lead_seventh_tower
  rel maud +small
  mood -small
  hs_escalation_progress
  say: "Seven towers, seven locks, one in each," she says. "When a tower goes dark, so does its lock." She looks at the Lecture Tower. "Locks can be mended. They need hands, and they need a key, and she knows it."

@event hs_two_shadows
title: Two Wands on the Ice
class: story
tone: tense
weight: 20
art: lantern
tags: mystery hollowstar
thread: hs_escalation
# v2: a confrontation on the page (style.md, "Conflict and climax"); it brings the invitations (hs_choosing_sides).
scene: Dusk on a half-frozen lake, two figures facing each other in the middle of the ice with wands raised, one holding a lantern, the dark tower behind them.
text: At dusk the headmistress and Kael walk out onto the frozen half of the lake from opposite shores and meet in the middle. Kael's voice carries all the way to the towers: "You'll seal it with students standing in the door!" Hers never rises, and carries anyway: "Better than your mother's way." Both wands come up. For a long moment nobody moves. Then she lowers hers first, and they part in silence.
> left: Ask Kael what they said
  rel kael +small
  mood -tiny
  queue hs_choosing_sides in 1
  say: "She wants the door shut her way. I want it shut mine." He stirs his tea until it freezes. "She asked about you. So did I. Don't make that face. You'll be asked."
> right: Ask the headmistress
  meet isolde
  rel isolde +small
  rel kael -tiny
  queue hs_choosing_sides in 1
  say: "We disagree about method," she says, "and agree about the door." She studies you as if you were a chess problem. "Expect an invitation. Possibly two. Choose with your eyes open." Kael, across the hall, sees you leave her tower.

@event hs_choosing_sides
title: Two Invitations
when: seen(hs_two_shadows) > 0
type: menu
class: story
tone: tense
weight: 20
art: letter
tags: mystery hollowstar
thread: hs_escalation
scene: A crowded refectory gone quiet, a student at a table between a tall woman in dark robes and a pale young man, both waiting for an answer.
text: Two invitations, both in front of the whole refectory. The headmistress, passing your table: "My study, after supper. Come alone. There will be chess." And Kael, not ten seconds later, loud enough for her to hear: "She wants you in her circle. I know the door from the other side. Come with us." Every head in the hall turns to you.
> wardens: Join the headmistress's circle
  hint: The Wardens: old rules, old wards.
  flag sided_wardens
  rel isolde +large
  rel kael -small
  lore +small
  hs_escalation_progress
  say: She beats you at chess in eleven moves, then tells you about the seal while she resets the board. "Rings are for people who have stood on the ice," she says. "Until then, you have my door."
> dumonts: Stand with the Dumonts
  hint: Kael's way, against his own family.
  flag sided_dumonts
  rel kael +large
  rel isolde -small
  if met(ilse):
    rel ilse +small
  arcana +small
  hs_escalation_progress
  say: "Not my family," Kael says, to the whole hall. "Us." He teaches you to hold a ward in a wind that wants your fingers. His hands are cold. They are steadier than yours.
> self: Go my own way
  hint: Nobody's circle. Nobody's help.
  flag sided_self
  guile +small
  lore +small
  mood -small
  hs_escalation_progress
  say: You thank them both, out loud, and keep your own notes in your own cipher. It's lonelier than you expected. Both of them, you notice, keep an eye on you anyway.
> none: Stay out of it
  hint: It isn't your door.
  mood +small
  rel kael -tiny
  say: You turn both invitations down. Kael nods as if he expected it. The headmistress's note simply says, the next morning, "Understood. Mind the ice."

# ---------------- Act IV: convergence ----------------

@event hs_last_winter
title: The Last Winter Before
arc: hollowstar
beat: 10
when: final_year and (clues(hollowstar) >= 2 or flag(sided_wardens) or flag(sided_dumonts) or flag(sided_self) or flag(warden_trial))
type: menu
class: story
tone: tense
art: lantern
tags: mystery hollowstar
thread: hs_convergence
# Act IV's opener (v2): each ally says it out loud. Whoever you train with will come down with you on the Night, even
# if you go early (hs_night_company, night_* in threads.grim).
scene: Lantern light in a frost-rimed window, the frozen edge of the lake beyond it, a student's desk covered in maps of seven towers.
text: The Lecture Tower has been dark for a year, and the lake freezes overnight in circles now. In spring the seal will be at its weakest. In the same week, one after another, they come and say it plainly: they'll stand with you beneath the lake, if you'll have them. You have one winter, and evenings enough for one of them.
> kael: Train with Kael on the ice
  hint: He'll come down with you, and fight beside you.
  flag winter_kael
  rel kael +large
  health -small
  say: He drills you on the ice until you can hold a ward with numb hands. "Again," he says, and then, quietly, "Good." You will remember that he said it.
> maud: Mend wards with Maud
  hint: She'll come down with you, and knows the founders' wall.
  flag winter_maud
  rel maud +large
  mood -small
  say: You walk the towers with her, tracing old wards back into the stone. "Your hands are steadier than mine were," she says, and doesn't say whose hands she means.
> isolde: Study with the headmistress
  hint: She'll come down with you; you'll know the founders' words.
  flag winter_isolde
  rel isolde +large
  lore +small
  mood -small
  say: You lose at chess every evening and learn the founders' words between moves. Once you nearly win. Her short, delighted laugh is the warmest sound you hear all winter.
> ilse: Spar with Ilse at the shore
  hint: She'll come down with you, and fight beside you.
  when: met(ilse) and not flag(ilse_taken) and not flag(ilse_went_north)
  flag winter_ilse
  rel ilse +large
  health -small
  say: She knocks you into the snow eleven times. The twelfth time you don't fall, and she looks at you as if you had done a trick she has never learned the counter to.
> alone: Rest while you still can
  hint: A quiet winter. No new training, but rested.
  rest
  say: You sleep, you eat, you read novels with no doors in them. It's the kindest winter you've had in years, and you can feel the lake getting colder anyway.

@event hs_ilse_door
title: What Ilse Was Taught
when: met(ilse) and not clue(ilse_truth) and not flag(ilse_taken) and not flag(ilse_went_north)
actor: ilse
class: story
tone: grim
art: door
tags: mystery hollowstar
weight: 14
thread: hs_investigation
scene: A young woman in white furs drawing a round door in the snow with the tip of a wand, a frozen lake behind her.
text: Ilse draws a circle in the snow with her wand, then a smaller one inside it. "This is the door," she says. "I have drawn it every day since I was six. I have never seen it." She doesn't look up. "Ask me what they taught me to do. Or don't. I don't care which."
> left: "What did they teach you?"
  flag ilse_confided
  find ilse_truth
  rel ilse +small
  hs_investigation_progress
  mood -small
  say: She tells you, flatly, like a lesson recited: how to stand, what to say, where to put her hands. "They raised me to open it," she says. "Nobody asked me if I wanted to." Then, sharply: "Now you know. Don't look at me like that."
> right: "You don't have to tell me."
  rel ilse +medium
  mood -tiny
  say: She rubs the circle out with her boot. "Kindness," she says, as if naming a trick. "I haven't learned the counter to that one yet." She doesn't leave, though.
